{"id":"mahabharata-5-070","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":70,"title":"सप्ततितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 70 · Yudhishthira asks Krishna to go as envoy","summary":{"en":"After Sanjaya's departure Yudhishthira tells Krishna that the Kauravas will not even grant five villages, and that a Kshatriya can live only by fighting, yet war among kin is evil. He asks Krishna's counsel, and Krishna resolves to go himself to the Kuru court to seek peace without sacrificing the Pandavas' rights.","kn":"ಸಂಜಯನು ಹೋದ ಮೇಲೆ ಕೌರವರು ಐದು ಗ್ರಾಮಗಳನ್ನೂ ಕೊಡರು, ಕ್ಷತ್ರಿಯನು ಹೋರಾಡಿಯೇ ಬದುಕಬೇಕು, ಆದರೆ ಬಂಧುಗಳ ಯುದ್ಧ ಪಾಪ ಎಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಸಲಹೆ ಕೇಳಿದಾಗ ಪಾಂಡವರ ಹಕ್ಕು ಬಿಡದೆ ಶಾಂತಿ ಕೋರಲು ತಾನೇ ಕುರುಸಭೆಗೆ ಹೋಗುವೆನೆಂದು ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನು ನಿಶ್ಚಯಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"सञ्जय के जाने के बाद युधिष्ठिर श्रीकृष्ण से कहते हैं कि कौरव पाँच गाँव भी नहीं देंगे, और क्षत्रिय युद्ध से ही जीता है, फिर भी बन्धुओं में युद्ध पाप है। वे श्रीकृष्ण की सलाह माँगते हैं, और श्रीकृष्ण पाण्डवों के अधिकार छोड़े बिना शान्ति माँगने स्वयं कुरु सभा में जाने का निश्चय करते हैं।","te":"సంజయుడు వెళ్లిన తర్వాత కౌరవులు ఐదు గ్రామాలు కూడా ఇవ్వరని, క్షత్రియుడు పోరాడే జీవించాలని, అయినా బంధువుల యుద్ధం పాపమని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు శ్రీకృష్ణునికి చెబుతాడు. సలహా అడగగా పాండవుల హక్కులను వదలకుండా శాంతి కోరడానికి తానే కురుసభకు వెళ్తానని శ్రీకృష్ణుడు నిశ్చయిస్తాడు.","ta":"ஸஞ்ஜயன் சென்றபின் கௌரவர்கள் ஐந்து கிராமங்களையும் தர மாட்டார்கள், க்ஷத்ரியன் போரிட்டே வாழ வேண்டும், ஆனால் உறவினரிடையே போர் தீயது என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணரிடம் சொல்கிறார். அவர் அறிவுரை கேட்க, பாண்டவர்களின் உரிமையை விட்டுக்கொடுக்காமல் அமைதி நாடத் தாமே குரு சபைக்குச் செல்வதாக ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர் தீர்மானிக்கிறார்.","ml":"സഞ്ജയൻ മടങ്ങിയശേഷം, കൗരവർ അഞ്ചു ഗ്രാമം പോലും തരില്ലെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ കൃഷ്ണനോട് പറയുന്നു; ക്ഷത്രിയന് യുദ്ധം ചെയ്താണ് ജീവിക്കാനാകുന്നതെങ്കിലും, ബന്ധുക്കൾ തമ്മിലുള്ള യുദ്ധം തിന്മയാണ്. അദ്ദേഹം കൃഷ്ണന്റെ ഉപദേശം ചോദിക്കുന്നു; പാണ്ഡവരുടെ അവകാശം ബലികഴിക്കാതെ സമാധാനം തേടി, കുരുസഭയിലേക്ക് താൻ തന്നെ പോകാൻ കൃഷ്ണൻ തീരുമാനിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.70; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"भगवद्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Bhagavadyana Parva (Krishna's embassy)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"संजये प्रतियाते तु धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nअभ्यभाषत दाशार्हमृषभं सर्वसात्वताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Sanjaya had left, Yudhishthira, king of dharma, spoke to Dasharha Krishna, bull of all the Sattvatas."}},{"n":2,"text":"अयं स कालः संप्राप्तो मित्राणां मे जनार्दन ।\nन च त्वदन्यं पश्यामि यो न आपत्सु तारयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Janardana, this is the time that has come for my friends; I see no one but you who could save us in calamities."}},{"n":3,"text":"त्वां हि माधव संश्रित्य निर्भया मोहदर्पितम् ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रं सहामात्यं स्वमंशमनुयुञ्ज्महे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Relying on you, Madhava, fearless, we claim our own share from Dhritarashtra's son, who is deluded by pride, along with his ministers."}},{"n":4,"text":"यथा हि सर्वास्वापत्सु पासि वृष्णीनरिंदम ।\nतथा ते पाण्डवा रक्ष्याः पाह्यस्मान्महतो भयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As you protect the Vrishnis in all calamities, tamer of foes, so the Pandavas must be protected by you; protect us from this great fear."}},{"text":"भगवानुवाच","meaning":{"en":"The Blessed Lord said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"अयमस्मि महाबाहो ब्रूहि यत्ते विवक्षितम् ।\nकरिष्यामि हि तत्सर्वं यत्त्वं वक्ष्यसि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here I am, mighty-armed one; say what you wish to say; I shall do all that you say, Bharata."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"श्रुतं ते धृतराष्ट्रस्य सपुत्रस्य चिकीर्षितम् ।\nएतद्धि सकलं कृष्ण संजयो मां यदब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have heard what Dhritarashtra and his sons want to do, Krishna; Sanjaya told me all of it."}},{"n":7,"text":"तन्मतं धृतराष्ट्रस्य सोऽस्यात्मा विवृतान्तरः ।\nयथोक्तं दूत आचष्टे वध्यः स्यादन्यथा ब्रुवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That is Dhritarashtra's opinion, for he is Dhritarashtra's very self with the veil lifted; a messenger tells as told, and would deserve death if he spoke otherwise."}},{"n":8,"text":"अप्रदानेन राज्यस्य शान्तिमस्मासु मार्गति ।\nलुब्धः पापेन मनसा चरन्नसममात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By not giving the kingdom he seeks peace with us, greedy and walking with a sinful mind that is not even with itself."}},{"n":9,"text":"यत्तद्द्वादश वर्षाणि वने निर्व्युषिता वयम् ।\nछद्मना शरदं चैकां धृतराष्ट्रस्य शासनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For twelve years we lived in the forest and one year in disguise at Dhritarashtra's command."}},{"n":10,"text":"स्थाता नः समये तस्मिन्धृतराष्ट्र इति प्रभो ।\nनाहास्म समयं कृष्ण तद्धि नो ब्राह्मणा विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord Krishna, we did not break the agreement, as Brahmins know; Dhritarashtra was to stand by it."}},{"n":11,"text":"वृद्धो राजा धृतराष्ट्रः स्वधर्मं नानुपश्यति ।\nपश्यन्वा पुत्रगृद्धित्वान्मन्दस्यान्वेति शासनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Old King Dhritarashtra does not see his own dharma; or seeing it, out of attachment to his son, he follows the command of the dull one."}},{"n":12,"text":"सुयोधनमते तिष्ठन्राजास्मासु जनार्दन ।\nमिथ्या चरति लुब्धः संश्चरन्प्रियमिवात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king stays by Suyodhana's mind against us, Janardana, acting falsely and greedily, as if doing something dear to himself."}},{"n":13,"text":"इतो दुःखतरं किं नु यत्राहं मातरं ततः ।\nसंविधातुं न शक्नोमि मित्राणां वा जनार्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"What is more painful than this: that I cannot provide for my mother or my friends?"}},{"n":14,"text":"काशिभिश्चेदिपाञ्चालैर्मत्स्यैश्च मधुसूदन ।\nभवता चैव नाथेन पञ्च ग्रामा वृता मया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhusudana, with the Kashis, Chedis, Panchalas, Matsyas and you as protector, I have asked for five villages."}},{"n":15,"text":"कुशस्थलं वृकस्थलमासन्दी वारणावतम् ।\nअवसानं च गोविन्द किंचिदेवात्र पञ्चमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kushasthala, Vrikasthala, Asandi, Varanavata, and some fifth one besides, Govinda."}},{"n":16,"text":"पञ्च नस्तात दीयन्तां ग्रामा वा नगराणि वा ।\nवसेम सहिता येषु मा च नो भरता नशन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Give us five villages or towns, dear, where we may live together and not have the Bharatas perish.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"न च तानपि दुष्टात्मा धार्तराष्ट्रोऽनुमन्यते ।\nस्वाम्यमात्मनि मत्वासावतो दुःखतरं नु किम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But even that the evil-minded son of Dhritarashtra does not agree to, thinking himself lord of everything; what is more painful than this?"}},{"n":18,"text":"कुले जातस्य वृद्धस्य परवित्तेषु गृध्यतः ।\nलोभः प्रज्ञानमाहन्ति प्रज्ञा हन्ति हता ह्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one born in a good family, old, and greedy for others' wealth, greed destroys wisdom, wisdom when destroyed destroys modesty,"}},{"n":19,"text":"ह्रीर्हता बाधते धर्मं धर्मो हन्ति हतः श्रियम् ।\nश्रीर्हता पुरुषं हन्ति पुरुषस्यास्वता वधः ॥","meaning":{"en":"modesty destroyed harms dharma, dharma destroyed destroys prosperity, prosperity destroyed destroys a man; for a man, poverty is death."}},{"n":20,"text":"अस्वतो हि निवर्तन्ते ज्ञातयः सुहृदर्त्विजः ।\nअपुष्पादफलाद्वृक्षाद्यथा तात पतत्रिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Relatives, friends and priests turn away from the poor man, as birds from a tree without flower or fruit, dear."}},{"n":21,"text":"एतच्च मरणं तात यदस्मात्पतितादिव ।\nज्ञातयो विनिवर्तन्ते प्रेतसत्त्वादिवासवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This itself is death, that kin turn away from him as if he had fallen, as the gods from one who has died."}},{"n":22,"text":"नातः पापीयसीं कांचिदवस्थां शम्बरोऽब्रवीत् ।\nयत्र नैवाद्य न प्रातर्भोजनं प्रतिदृश्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shambara said there is no worse state than that in which neither today nor tomorrow a meal is seen."}},{"n":23,"text":"धनमाहुः परं धर्मं धने सर्वं प्रतिष्ठितम् ।\nजीवन्ति धनिनो लोके मृता ये त्वधना नराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They say wealth is the highest dharma, everything rests on wealth; those who have wealth live in the world, and the poor are dead."}},{"n":24,"text":"ये धनादपकर्षन्ति नरं स्वबलमाश्रिताः ।\nते धर्ममर्थं कामं च प्रमथ्नन्ति नरं च तम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who, relying on their own strength, pull a man away from wealth crush his dharma, profit and desire, and the man himself."}},{"n":25,"text":"एतामवस्थां प्राप्यैके मरणं वव्रिरे जनाः ।\nग्रामायैके वनायैके नाशायैके प्रवव्रजुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching this state, some choose death; some go off to villages, some to the forest, some to ruin."}},{"n":26,"text":"उन्मादमेके पुष्यन्ति यान्त्यन्ये द्विषतां वशम् ।\nदास्यमेके निगच्छन्ति परेषामर्थहेतुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some foster madness, others come under their enemies' power, others fall into servitude to others for gain."}},{"n":27,"text":"आपदेवास्य मरणात्पुरुषस्य गरीयसी ।\nश्रियो विनाशस्तद्ध्यस्य निमित्तं धर्मकामयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Calamity is graver for a man than death itself: the loss of prosperity is the cause of the loss of dharma and desire."}},{"n":28,"text":"यदस्य धर्म्यं मरणं शाश्वतं लोकवर्त्म तत् ।\nसमन्तात्सर्वभूतानां न तदत्येति कश्चन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Death for a dharmic man is the eternal way of the world for all beings; nobody escapes it."}},{"n":29,"text":"न तथा बाध्यते कृष्ण प्रकृत्या निर्धनो जनः ।\nयथा भद्रां श्रियं प्राप्य तया हीनः सुखैधितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, a poor man is not so troubled by his nature as one who, having gained fair fortune and then lost it, had grown up in comfort."}},{"n":30,"text":"स तदात्मापराधेन संप्राप्तो व्यसनं महत् ।\nसेन्द्रान्गर्हयते देवान्नात्मानं च कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brought by his own fault into great misery, he blames the gods with Indra, never himself."}},{"n":31,"text":"न चास्मिन्सर्वशास्त्राणि प्रतरन्ति निगर्हणाम् ।\nसोऽभिक्रुध्यति भृत्यानां सुहृदश्चाभ्यसूयति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Not all the scriptures bring him past this reproach; he gets angry at his servants and resents his friends."}},{"n":32,"text":"तं तदा मन्युरेवैति स भूयः संप्रमुह्यति ।\nस मोहवशमापन्नः क्रूरं कर्म निषेवते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then anger itself comes to him and he is deluded again; fallen under delusion, he practises cruel deeds."}},{"n":33,"text":"पापकर्मात्ययायैव संकरं तेन पुष्यति ।\nसंकरो नरकायैव सा काष्ठा पापकर्मणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He feeds confusion for the sake of sinful acts; confusion leads only to hell; that is the end of sinful deeds."}},{"n":34,"text":"न चेत्प्रबुध्यते कृष्ण नरकायैव गच्छति ।\nतस्य प्रबोधः प्रज्ञैव प्रज्ञाचक्षुर्न रिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"If he does not awaken, Krishna, he goes only to hell; his awakening is wisdom itself, and the one with wisdom as eyes does not perish."}},{"n":35,"text":"प्रज्ञालाभे हि पुरुषः शास्त्राण्येवान्ववेक्षते ।\nशास्त्रनित्यः पुनर्धर्मं तस्य ह्रीरङ्गमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When wisdom is gained, a man looks to the scriptures; steady in the scriptures, again to dharma; modesty is his highest limb."}},{"n":36,"text":"ह्रीमान्हि पापं प्रद्वेष्टि तस्य श्रीरभिवर्धते ।\nश्रीमान्स यावद्भवति तावद्भवति पूरुषः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The modest man hates sin and his fortune grows; as long as he is prosperous, he is a man."}},{"n":37,"text":"धर्मनित्यः प्रशान्तात्मा कार्ययोगवहः सदा ।\nनाधर्मे कुरुते बुद्धिं न च पापेषु वर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Steady in dharma, calm in mind, always bearing the work of duty, he sets his mind not on adharma and does not engage in sin."}},{"n":38,"text":"अह्रीको वा विमूढो वा नैव स्त्री न पुनः पुमान् ।\nनास्याधिकारो धर्मेऽस्ति यथा शूद्रस्तथैव सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One without shame or one deluded is neither woman nor man; he has no claim in dharma, he is like a shudra."}},{"n":39,"text":"ह्रीमानवति देवांश्च पितॄनात्मानमेव च ।\nतेनामृतत्वं व्रजति सा काष्ठा पुण्यकर्मणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The modest one protects the gods, the ancestors and himself, and so goes to immortality; that is the goal of virtuous deeds."}},{"n":40,"text":"तदिदं मयि ते दृष्टं प्रत्यक्षं मधुसूदन ।\nयथा राज्यात्परिभ्रष्टो वसामि वसतीरिमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is what you see in me directly, Madhusudana, fallen from my kingdom, living in these dwellings."}},{"n":41,"text":"ते वयं न श्रियं हातुमलं न्यायेन केनचित् ।\nअत्र नो यतमानानां वधश्चेदपि साधु तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We are not able to give up fortune by any rightful means; if in striving for it we are killed, that too is good."}},{"n":42,"text":"तत्र नः प्रथमः कल्पो यद्वयं ते च माधव ।\nप्रशान्ताः समभूताश्च श्रियं तामश्नुवीमहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Our first course, Madhava, is that we and they become calm and equal and enjoy that fortune."}},{"n":43,"text":"तत्रैषा परमा काष्ठा रौद्रकर्मक्षयोदया ।\nयद्वयं कौरवान्हत्वा तानि राष्ट्राण्यशीमहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The highest course then, the end that arises from cruel deeds, is that we kill the Kauravas and eat those kingdoms."}},{"n":44,"text":"ये पुनः स्युरसंबद्धा अनार्याः कृष्ण शत्रवः ।\nतेषामप्यवधः कार्यः किं पुनर्ये स्युरीदृशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even enemies unrelated and ignoble, Krishna, should not be killed; how much less those who are such as these?"}},{"n":45,"text":"ज्ञातयश्च हि भूयिष्ठाः सहाया गुरवश्च नः ।\nतेषां वधोऽतिपापीयान्किं नु युद्धेऽस्ति शोभनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Most of them are our kin, helpers and elders; their killing is most sinful; what good is there in war?"}},{"n":46,"text":"पापः क्षत्रियधर्मोऽयं वयं च क्षत्रबान्धवाः ।\nस नः स्वधर्मोऽधर्मो वा वृत्तिरन्या विगर्हिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"This kshatriya dharma is sinful, and we are kshatriya kin; whether it is our own dharma or adharma, another livelihood is blamed."}},{"n":47,"text":"शूद्रः करोति शुश्रूषां वैश्या विपणिजीविनः ।\nवयं वधेन जीवामः कपालं ब्राह्मणैर्वृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A shudra gives service, vaishyas live by trade; we live by killing; a Brahmin's skull-bowl is the beggar's."}},{"n":48,"text":"क्षत्रियः क्षत्रियं हन्ति मत्स्यो मत्स्येन जीवति ।\nश्वा श्वानं हन्ति दाशार्ह पश्य धर्मो यथागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A kshatriya kills a kshatriya, a fish lives by a fish, a dog kills a dog, Dasharha; see how dharma has come."}},{"n":49,"text":"युद्धे कृष्ण कलिर्नित्यं प्राणाः सीदन्ति संयुगे ।\nबलं तु नीतिमात्राय हठे जयपराजयौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"In war, Krishna, there is always strife, lives are lost in battle; strength serves only policy, and victory and defeat are by chance."}},{"n":50,"text":"नात्मच्छन्देन भूतानां जीवितं मरणं तथा ।\nनाप्यकाले सुखं प्राप्यं दुःखं वापि यदूत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither life nor death of beings is by their own will, nor can happiness or sorrow be gained out of season, best of the Yadus."}},{"n":51,"text":"एको ह्यपि बहून्हन्ति घ्नन्त्येकं बहवोऽप्युत ।\nशूरं कापुरुषो हन्ति अयशस्वी यशस्विनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One kills many, and many kill one; a coward kills a hero and an infamous man a famous one."}},{"n":52,"text":"जयश्चैवोभयोर्दृष्ट उभयोश्च पराजयः ।\nतथैवापचयो दृष्टो व्यपयाने क्षयव्ययौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Victory and defeat are both seen for both sides, and loss and expense too are seen in retreat."}},{"n":53,"text":"सर्वथा वृजिनं युद्धं को घ्नन्न प्रतिहन्यते ।\nहतस्य च हृषीकेश समौ जयपराजयौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"War is wickedness in every way; who, killing, is not killed? And for the slain, Hrishikesha, victory and defeat are equal."}},{"n":54,"text":"पराजयश्च मरणान्मन्ये नैव विशिष्यते ।\nयस्य स्याद्विजयः कृष्ण तस्याप्यपचयो ध्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think defeat is no different from death; even for the one who wins, Krishna, there is certain loss."}},{"n":55,"text":"अन्ततो दयितं घ्नन्ति केचिदप्यपरे जनाः ।\nतस्याङ्ग बलहीनस्य पुत्रान्भ्रातॄनपश्यतः ।\nनिर्वेदो जीविते कृष्ण सर्वतश्चोपजायते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some people, in the end, kill even a beloved; and for a man weakened, who sees his sons and brothers slain, disgust with life arises everywhere."}},{"n":56,"text":"ये ह्येव वीरा ह्रीमन्त आर्याः करुणवेदिनः ।\nत एव युद्धे हन्यन्ते यवीयान्मुच्यते जनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who are heroes, modest, noble and knowing compassion are the very ones killed in war; the lesser people are spared."}},{"n":57,"text":"हत्वाप्यनुशयो नित्यं परानपि जनार्दन ।\nअनुबन्धश्च पापोऽत्र शेषश्चाप्यवशिष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even after killing, there is constant remorse, Janardana, for the others too; and a sinful bond follows, and a remnant remains."}},{"n":58,"text":"शेषो हि बलमासाद्य न शेषमवशेषयेत् ।\nसर्वोच्छेदे च यतते वैरस्यान्तविधित्सया ॥","meaning":{"en":"A remnant, having gained strength, would not leave a remnant; it strives for total destruction, wishing to end the enmity."}},{"n":59,"text":"जयो वैरं प्रसृजति दुःखमास्ते पराजितः ।\nसुखं प्रशान्तः स्वपिति हित्वा जयपराजयौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Victory breeds enmity; the defeated lives in sorrow; the peaceful sleep in happiness, having given up victory and defeat."}},{"n":60,"text":"जातवैरश्च पुरुषो दुःखं स्वपिति नित्यदा ।\nअनिर्वृतेन मनसा ससर्प इव वेश्मनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who has made an enemy sleeps in sorrow always, with unquiet mind, as if with a snake in the house."}},{"n":61,"text":"उत्सादयति यः सर्वं यशसा स वियुज्यते ।\nअकीर्तिं सर्वभूतेषु शाश्वतीं स नियच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who destroys everything is cut off from fame; he earns lasting infamy among all beings."}},{"n":62,"text":"न हि वैराणि शाम्यन्ति दीर्घकालकृतान्यपि ।\nआख्यातारश्च विद्यन्ते पुमांश्चोत्पद्यते कुले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Enmities, even long made, do not subside; there are those who retell them, and a man is born in the family."}},{"n":63,"text":"न चापि वैरं वैरेण केशव व्युपशाम्यति ।\nहविषाग्निर्यथा कृष्ण भूय एवाभिवर्धते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nor does enmity subside through enmity, Keshava; like fire with ghee, it only grows greater."}},{"n":64,"text":"अतोऽन्यथा नास्ति शान्तिर्नित्यमन्तरमन्ततः ।\nअन्तरं लिप्समानानामयं दोषो निरन्तरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is no peace otherwise, for ever seeking an opening in the end; this fault is constant for those who look for openings."}},{"n":65,"text":"पौरुषेयो हि बलवानाधिर्हृदयबाधनः ।\nतस्य त्यागेन वा शान्तिर्निवृत्त्या मनसोऽपि वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The strong mental affliction of man torments the heart; peace comes by giving it up or by turning the mind back."}},{"n":66,"text":"अथ वा मूलघातेन द्विषतां मधुसूदन ।\nफलनिर्वृत्तिरिद्धा स्यात्तन्नृशंसतरं भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or by destroying the enemies at the root, Madhusudana, the full fruit would arise, but that would be crueller."}},{"n":67,"text":"या तु त्यागेन शान्तिः स्यात्तदृते वध एव सः ।\nसंशयाच्च समुच्छेदाद्द्विषतामात्मनस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Peace that comes by giving up is, without it, only killing, from doubt and the complete destruction of enemies and oneself."}},{"n":68,"text":"न च त्यक्तुं तदिच्छामो न चेच्छामः कुलक्षयम् ।\nअत्र या प्रणिपातेन शान्तिः सैव गरीयसी ॥","meaning":{"en":"We neither wish to give it up nor wish the family's ruin; here peace by bowing down is the greater."}},{"n":69,"text":"सर्वथा यतमानानामयुद्धमभिकाङ्क्षताम् ।\nसान्त्वे प्रतिहते युद्धं प्रसिद्धमपराक्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For those who strive in every way and wish for no war, when conciliation is met with rebuff, war comes, famed and without valour."}},{"n":70,"text":"प्रतिघातेन सान्त्वस्य दारुणं संप्रवर्तते ।\nतच्छुनामिव गोपादे पण्डितैरुपलक्षितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When conciliation is repulsed, a terrible fight begins, like that of dogs at a cow's footprint, as the wise observe."}},{"n":71,"text":"लाङ्गूलचालनं क्ष्वेडः प्रतिरावो विवर्तनम् ।\nदन्तदर्शनमारावस्ततो युद्धं प्रवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wagging tails, growls, answering barks, circling, showing teeth and howling, and then the fight begins."}},{"n":72,"text":"तत्र यो बलवान्कृष्ण जित्वा सोऽत्ति तदामिषम् ।\nएवमेव मनुष्येषु विशेषो नास्ति कश्चन ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the stronger one wins and eats the meat, Krishna; among men too there is no difference."}},{"n":73,"text":"सर्वथा त्वेतदुचितं दुर्बलेषु बलीयसाम् ।\nअनादरो विरोधश्च प्रणिपाती हि दुर्बलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But it is right in every way that the strong show disregard and opposition to the weak, for the weak one bows."}},{"n":74,"text":"पिता राजा च वृद्धश्च सर्वथा मानमर्हति ।\nतस्मान्मान्यश्च पूज्यश्च धृतराष्ट्रो जनार्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Father, king and elder, he deserves honour in every way; so Dhritarashtra is to be honoured and respected, Janardana."}},{"n":75,"text":"पुत्रस्नेहस्तु बलवान्धृतराष्ट्रस्य माधव ।\nस पुत्रवशमापन्नः प्रणिपातं प्रहास्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra's love for his son is strong, Madhava; falling under his son's sway, he will give up bowing down."}},{"n":76,"text":"तत्र किं मन्यसे कृष्ण प्राप्तकालमनन्तरम् ।\nकथमर्थाच्च धर्माच्च न हीयेमहि माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"What do you think is timely next, Krishna? How could we not lose profit and dharma, Madhava?"}},{"n":77,"text":"ईदृशे ह्यर्थकृच्छ्रेऽस्मिन्कमन्यं मधुसूदन ।\nउपसंप्रष्टुमर्हामि त्वामृते पुरुषोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"In such a hard matter of profit, Madhusudana, whom else should I ask but you, supreme person?"}},{"n":78,"text":"प्रियश्च प्रियकामश्च गतिज्ञः सर्वकर्मणाम् ।\nको हि कृष्णास्ति नस्त्वादृक्सर्वनिश्चयवित्सुहृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear to us and wishing our good, knowing the path of all actions, who is there like you, Krishna, a friend who knows all decisions?"}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":79,"text":"एवमुक्तः प्रत्युवाच धर्मराजं जनार्दनः ।\nउभयोरेव वामर्थे यास्यामि कुरुसंसदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, Janardana replied to the king of dharma: \"I shall go to the Kuru assembly for both your sakes."}},{"n":80,"text":"शमं तत्र लभेयं चेद्युष्मदर्थमहापयन् ।\nपुण्यं मे सुमहद्राजंश्चरितं स्यान्महाफलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If I can gain peace there without harming your interests, great king, my deed will be very meritorious with great reward."}},{"n":81,"text":"मोचयेयं मृत्युपाशात्संरब्धान्कुरुसृञ्जयान् ।\nपाण्डवान्धार्तराष्ट्रांश्च सर्वां च पृथिवीमिमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I would free the Kurus and Srinjayas, enraged, from the snare of death, the Pandavas and Dhritarashtra's sons and this whole earth.\""}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":82,"text":"न ममैतन्मतं कृष्ण यत्त्वं यायाः कुरून्प्रति ।\nसुयोधनः सूक्तमपि न करिष्यति ते वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, this is not my wish, that you go to the Kurus; Suyodhana will not do your words even if well spoken."}},{"n":83,"text":"समेतं पार्थिवं क्षत्रं सुयोधनवशानुगम् ।\nतेषां मध्यावतरणं तव कृष्ण न रोचये ॥","meaning":{"en":"The assembled kshatriya kings follow Suyodhana's will; I do not like you stepping into the midst of them, Krishna."}},{"n":84,"text":"न हि नः प्रीणयेद्द्रव्यं न देवत्वं कुतः सुखम् ।\nन च सर्वामरैश्वर्यं तव रोधेन माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"No wealth would please us, nor godhood, much less happiness, nor sovereignty over all the immortals, Madhava, at the cost of your harm."}},{"text":"भगवानुवाच","meaning":{"en":"The Blessed Lord said:"}},{"n":85,"text":"जानाम्येतां महाराज धार्तराष्ट्रस्य पापताम् ।\nअवाच्यास्तु भविष्यामः सर्वलोके महीक्षिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I know this wickedness of Dhritarashtra's son, great king; but we shall be beyond reproach among all kings of the world."}},{"n":86,"text":"न चापि मम पर्याप्ताः सहिताः सर्वपार्थिवाः ।\nक्रुद्धस्य प्रमुखे स्थातुं सिंहस्येवेतरे मृगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nor are all the kings together enough to stand before me in my anger, as other animals before a lion."}},{"n":87,"text":"अथ चेत्ते प्रवर्तेरन्मयि किंचिदसांप्रतम् ।\nनिर्दहेयं कुरून्सर्वानिति मे धीयते मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And if they should do me any improper thing, my mind is set on burning all the Kurus."}},{"n":88,"text":"न जातु गमनं तत्र भवेत्पार्थ निरर्थकम् ।\nअर्थप्राप्तिः कदाचित्स्यादन्ततो वाप्यवाच्यता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going there will never be pointless, Partha; either something will be gained, or at the end there will be no blame."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":89,"text":"यत्तुभ्यं रोचते कृष्ण स्वस्ति प्राप्नुहि कौरवान् ।\nकृतार्थं स्वस्तिमन्तं त्वां द्रक्ष्यामि पुनरागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, go as pleases you, and attain well-being among the Kauravas; I shall see you return, successful and well."}},{"n":90,"text":"विष्वक्सेन कुरून्गत्वा भारताञ्शमयेः प्रभो ।\nयथा सर्वे सुमनसः सह स्यामः सुचेतसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vishvaksena, go to the Kurus and calm the Bharatas, lord, so that we may all be of good mind and good heart together."}},{"n":91,"text":"भ्राता चासि सखा चासि बीभत्सोर्मम च प्रियः ।\nसौहृदेनाविशङ्क्योऽसि स्वस्ति प्राप्नुहि भूतये ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are my brother and friend, dear to Bibhatsu and to me; you are beyond doubt by friendship; go and attain welfare for our prosperity."}},{"n":92,"text":"अस्मान्वेत्थ परान्वेत्थ वेत्थार्थं वेत्थ भाषितम् ।\nयद्यदस्मद्धितं कृष्ण तत्तद्वाच्यः सुयोधनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You know us, you know them, you know the goal and what is said; whatever is good for us, Krishna, that is what Suyodhana should be told."}},{"n":93,"text":"यद्यद्धर्मेण संयुक्तमुपपद्येद्धितं वचः ।\nतत्तत्केशव भाषेथाः सान्त्वं वा यदि वेतरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever speech is joined with dharma and suitable and good, Keshava, speak that, whether conciliatory or otherwise."}}]}]}